WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
A medieval king wears the crown.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.310
Surely nobody can tell him what to do?

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.210
Yet in eleven seventy,

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.510
Archbishop Thomas Becket was
murdered after clashing with King

5
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.910
Henry the Second.

6
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.570
And in twelve fifteen,

7
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.710
angry barons forced King John
to seal a great charter,

8
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.850
called Magna Carta.

9
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.850
So who really held power: the
king, the Church, or the barons?

10
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.050
And was a king above the law?

11
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.170
In this mission, you'll see
how the Church shaped everyday

12
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.230
life, and what Magna Carta really did.

13
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.230
You'll also meet the first
Parliament to summon townsmen.

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.740
Your mission: find out who could
limit a medieval king's power.
